<title>PHILIPPINES: Sumitomo, Hanjin win Manila rail deal.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo, Hanjin win Manila rail deal.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines Light Railway Transit (LRT) Authority on Monday confirmed the winning bids of Japan's Sumitomo Corp and Korea's Hanjin Heavy Industries for the city's LRT project.</p>
<p>The authority approved the 1.03 billion peso bid of Sumitomo for a depot facility, an LRT official said.</p>
<p>It also endorsed the award of the substructure component of the LRT line to a consortium of Hanjin and Itochu Corp, he said.</p>
<p>The Hanjin consortium put a bid of 2.752 billion pesos.  </p>
<p>The LRT said construction of the depot and the substructure component would begin this year.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
